# PathFuse — declaratively provision sbfd's runtime state directory.
#
# sbfd's unit already gets /run/sbfd via `RuntimeDirectory=sbfd`, but that is
# created ONCE, at service start, and torn down/recreated only across the
# service's own lifecycle. It runs as an unprivileged user, so if the directory
# is ever removed out from under the running daemon (a deploy that cleans up an
# adjacent unit, a stray operator command), the daemon cannot recreate it under
# root-owned /run and silently stops publishing state — and every downstream
# reader (the maintenance-reboot gate, sbfd-ctl) then reads blind.
#
# This rule makes the directory a first-class, declarative object: recreated at
# every boot and on demand via `systemd-tmpfiles --create`, independent of when
# (or whether) the daemon restarts. install.sh runs `--create` so a deploy that
# disturbs it puts it back before the deploy finishes.
d /run/sbfd 0755 $users_sbfd $users_sbfd -
